1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:03,720
Why does planning one team
lunch take so many messages?

2
00:00:03,790 --> 00:00:07,705
Introducing Teamfare. It helps
teams plan an outing, get approval,

3
00:00:07,730 --> 00:00:10,640
and keep track of spending, all in one place.

4
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:12,135
Let me show you how it works.

5
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:15,520
We're planning lunch for four
people in Victoria Island, Lagos.

6
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:18,115
We have twenty-two dollars and
twenty-eight cents per person

7
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:21,580
to spend. I start with a short
description of what we want.

8
00:00:21,660 --> 00:00:24,940
Then I enter the number of
people, the location, a date, and

9
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:28,585
our budget. When I'm ready,
I click Research options.

10
00:00:28,610 --> 00:00:31,705
Teamfare's AI searches the web
for places that could work.

11
00:00:31,730 --> 00:00:34,350
It brings back a few choices,
with links to the information

12
00:00:34,710 --> 00:00:37,875
it found. I can see the expected
cost and what each option

13
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:41,295
includes. Any price that still
needs checking is clearly marked

14
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:44,710
as an estimate. I choose a place,
and Teamfare turns it into

15
00:00:44,830 --> 00:00:48,715
a plan. The activities, guests,
and costs are together on one

16
00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:52,195
page. I can change the details
before sending it to anyone.

17
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:53,835
Next, let's find a time.

18
00:00:53,860 --> 00:00:57,305
I suggest two options. Each invited
teammate can tick the times

19
00:00:57,330 --> 00:01:00,565
that work for them. Teamfare shows
the replies, so I can choose

20
00:01:00,590 --> 00:01:02,885
a time based on what
people have actually said.

21
00:01:02,910 --> 00:01:04,690
Now I send the plan to our manager.

22
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:07,835
In their own account, they can
see the total cost, the cost

23
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:10,845
for each person, and how
much of the budget is left.

24
00:01:10,870 --> 00:01:13,595
They can ask for changes with
a note, or approve the plan.

25
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:17,060
After approval, teammates can
say they're coming and download

26
00:01:17,170 --> 00:01:18,585
an event for their calendar.

27
00:01:18,610 --> 00:01:22,080
Private teams can also turn on
email invitations and reminders.

28
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:25,420
These shared judge accounts have
outgoing emails switched off.

29
00:01:25,660 --> 00:01:27,325
Now let's record an expense.

30
00:01:27,350 --> 00:01:30,042
I enter a sample lunch cost of
eight dollars and ninety-one

31
00:01:30,067 --> 00:01:32,320
cents and attach a sample receipt.

32
00:01:32,380 --> 00:01:35,125
The expense stays linked to
this outing, so the manager can

33
00:01:35,150 --> 00:01:38,275
find it later. On the Expenses
page, the manager can choose

34
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:41,425
an outing and a date range, then
download the matching records

35
00:01:41,450 --> 00:01:43,990
as a spreadsheet. That makes it
easier to see what was spent

36
00:01:44,430 --> 00:01:47,575
and share a report. Teamfare runs on Vultr.

37
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:49,760
Vultr Cloud Compute hosts the app.

38
00:01:49,820 --> 00:01:52,845
Qwen is the AI model, and we
use it through Vultr Serverless

39
00:01:52,870 --> 00:01:55,405
Inference. Tavily handles web search.

40
00:01:55,430 --> 00:01:58,695
Vultr Object Storage keeps encrypted
backups to help us recover

41
00:01:58,720 --> 00:02:02,375
our data. Bookings and payments
still happen outside Teamfare.

42
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:06,045
Teamfare brings the planning, team
replies, approval, and spending

43
00:02:06,070 --> 00:02:08,700
records together. Bring your team together.

44
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:10,273
Leave the admin to us.
